{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:81552","published":"2026-10-12T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-10-29T11:32:38.306816807Z","related":["CVE-2026-46309","CVE-2026-63925","CVE-2026-64507","CVE-2026-64508","CVE-2026-68123","CVE-2026-68236","CVE-2026-68245","CVE-2026-68278","CVE-2026-72318","CVE-2026-80887","CVE-2026-89811","CVE-2026-89894","CVE-2026-89970"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-46309","CVE-2026-63925","CVE-2026-64507","CVE-2026-64508","CVE-2026-68123","CVE-2026-68236","CVE-2026-68245","CVE-2026-68278","CVE-2026-72318","CVE-2026-80887","CVE-2026-89811","CVE-2026-89894","CVE-2026-89970"],"summary":"Important: kernel security update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: drm/xe/uapi: Reject coh_none PAT index for CPU cached memory in madvise (CVE-2026-46309)\n  * kernel: macsec: fix replay protection at XPN lower-PN wrap (CVE-2026-63925)\n  * kernel: bpf: Support for hardening against JIT spraying (CVE-2026-64508)\n  * kernel: x86/bugs: Enable IBPB flush on BPF JIT allocation (CVE-2026-64507)\n  * kernel: drm/amd/display: set new_stream to NULL after release (CVE-2026-68236)\n  * kernel: drm/dp/mst: fix buffer overflows in sideband chunk accumulation (CVE-2026-68278)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu: fix lifetime issue of amdgpu_vm_get_task_info_pasid() (CVE-2026-68245)\n  * kernel: openvswitch: fix GSO userspace truncation underflow (CVE-2026-68123)\n  * kernel: cifs: validate DFS referral string offsets (CVE-2026-72318)\n  * kernel: drm/vmwgfx: use check_add_overflow for shader size+offset bound (CVE-2026-80887)\n  * kernel: nvmet-auth: Synchronize timeout work during SQ teardown (CVE-2026-89970)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Add TLB flush after MES queue eviction/suspension (CVE-2026-89811)\n  * kernel: media: cx231xx: reject geometry changes while the VBI queue is busy (CVE-2026-89894)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowle